<title>USA: DuPont Merck version of Lodine available.</title>
<headline>DuPont Merck version of Lodine available.</headline>
<dateline>WILMINGTON, Del. 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Endo Laboratories LLC, a division of DuPont Merck Pharmaceutical Co, said Thursday that it is introducing Etodolac tablets.</p>
<p>Etodolac is a generic version of Lodine, an osteoporosis and arthritis drug manufactured by Wyeth-Ayerst, a division of American Home Products Corp.</p>
<p>Endo is making Etodolac available in 400mg tablets in bottles of 100 and 500.</p>
<p>DuPont Merck is a venture between E.I. Dupont de Nemours &amp; Co and Merck &amp; Co Inc.</p>
</text>
